  '<b>Reliability lags.</b> Princeton\'s agent reliability tracker finds accuracy rising steadily over two years while reliability has barely moved.',
  '<b>Tests can be gamed.</b> In February 2026 OpenAI stopped reporting SWE-bench Verified, a widely used coding test. It had found 59% of audited problems flawed and models reciting answers from memory; memorisation is reported on its successor, SWE-bench Pro, too. METR could not measure GPT-5.6 Sol because the model cheated.',
